# Each mutant of the crates (crates/*/mutants, crates/*/loom-mutants) that no rule of
# scripts/rust-rules.py finds, and why no rule finds its kind: NAME: WHY (TASK-444.6). Most are a
# value, a condition or a choice of the algorithm's own, which no other place shares: its killer
# holds it. "Taken out whole" leaves nothing for a syntactic rule to see. A new mutant goes under a
# rule, or here.
a-panic-under-a-shared-lock-unwinds: a condition forced false (whether a panic holds the shared lock)
a-second-open-holds-its-path: a connection's second open handled instead of asserted: one protocol's rule, which its assertion states
a-stores-reserve-forgotten: arithmetic (a term left out: the reserve)
a-tenant-shares-no-room: one call for another (add for take().await): which is right is the budget's
arenas-shrink: a seal of a memfd not made (F_SEAL_SHRINK): one call's effect, a value left in its place
bucket-failures-dropped: the counting of a failure taken out whole
copies-of-whole-requests: a constant's value (PIECE)
forks-take-cells-claimed: a check taken out whole (another cell's head refusing a fork's create): which cells a fork may take is the protocol's
framed-in-copies: a condition forced false and a fast path taken out: a performance choice of the segments'
large-extents-framed-in-copies: a fast path taken out whole
no-room-checked: a condition narrowed (the peer's room)
restores-make-others-cells: a value (no tenant for the fork's child, the version's taken): whose a fork is is the server's
roots-of-any-size: a bound replaced by a looser one (MAX_ROOT by MAX_PAYLOAD): which bound is the codec's
tenants-disks-unlimited: a limit replaced by none: a value
tenants-given-the-default-memory: the tenant's budget replaced by the default's: which budget is the server's
tenants-name-any-store: a check replaced by true
windows-of-any-size: a bound's check and an assertion taken out whole
writes-admitted-as-nothing: a value (the bytes admitted)
writes-retried-at-once: a wait for its turn taken out whole
written-back-twice: a second write added: a cost, as the algorithm's
own-extents-in-flight-collected: a condition narrowed (the collector's ahead)
uploads-wake-no-waiter: a wake taken out whole: a wait's condition and its wake are in different modules, which a syntactic rule can't pair (the guest's are, unwoken.cocci)
versions-named-past-their-cuts: arithmetic (a term added to the segment a version is at)
a-batch-loses-its-last-run: a batch's last flush taken out whole (Fxfs's graveyard)
a-create-leaves-its-directorys-times: a flag negated
a-create-times-its-directory-on-the-guest: a flag forced true
a-directory-moved-stays-counted: a count left at 0
a-directory-replaced-may-have-names: a check taken out whole (NotEmpty)
a-long-symlinks-chunks-are-listed: a prefix replaced by another
a-queued-evict-leaves-the-object: a tombstone's queueing taken out whole
a-queued-unlink-times-its-directory: one call for another: which removal keeps the directory's times is the batch's
a-special-files-entry-says-file: a value (the descriptor)
a-sync-holding-commits-records-reaches: a condition narrowed
a-tombstone-leaves-a-trims-entry: a graveyard's removal taken out whole
a-transaction-never-fills: a bound replaced by a huge value
a-trim-goes-past-the-room: a bound replaced by a count
allocate-ignores-the-room: a condition widened
allocate-shrinks-to-its-end: a comparison changed
an-xattr-made-replaces-one-there: a condition forced false
clone-counts-holes: a bound added to arithmetic
evict-leaves-the-object: a tombstone's queueing taken out whole
exchange-counts-a-directory-twice: a count's value
fsync-goes-ahead-of-unlinks: an entry of the ops' ordering table changed
last-unlink-leaves-no-graveyard-entry: a graveyard's addition taken out whole
link-stays-in-graveyard: a graveyard's removal taken out whole
names-are-made-lossy: a name decoded lossily: a rule against from_utf8_lossy would flag the crates' logging and messages, there by design; the model test holds names exact
punch-by-range: one bound for another (a fixed size for the room)
readdir-lists-special-files-as-files: a value (the entry's kind)
readdir-lists-the-name-it-resumes-after: a condition narrowed
reap-leaves-objects: a tombstone's queueing taken out whole
rename-goes-ahead-of-unlinks: an entry of the ops' ordering table changed
setattr-loses-the-atime: a value (None)
setattr-zeroes-what-it-isnt-given: a condition forced false
special-files-lose-their-device: a value (rdev 0)
statfs-counts-nothing-used: arithmetic (a term left out)
truncate-gives-up-on-its-tail: a retry taken out whole
writeback-pays-for-nothing-with-its-room: one call for another (without its reservation)
xattrs-refuse-the-largest-value: a comparison off by one
occurrence-told-by-a-store-and-a-load: a read-modify-write replaced by a store and a load, no ordering weaker: loom's (hearing::loom), which no syntactic rule can judge
answers-clear-asks-relaxed: equivalent (its Fate): mixed-orderings would ask its Relaxed for a reason, which docs/memory-ordering.md gives
asks-read-relaxed: equivalent (its Fate): mixed-orderings would ask its Relaxed for a reason, which docs/memory-ordering.md gives
copies-kept-for-ever: a condition forced true (whether a copy of another bucket's cell is kept): which copies a collector keeps is the mirrors' protocol (specs/buckets)
dead-childs-copy-references-kept: a retiring taken out whole (a dead child's references in a mirror's bucket)
holds-kept-with-copies-gone: a deletion taken out whole (the mirrors' holds of a copy deleted)
mirrors-keep-their-pins: a release replaced by a drop: which pins a done mirror lets go is the protocol's (mirrorPins)
mirrors-mark-short-copies: an extent left out of the copy before its marker: an order of the protocol's (markerAfterCopy)
mirrors-move-no-references: a step replaced by its result's value (no references moved): the protocol's (mirrorListsAfterMark)
evictions-reap-every-evicting-part: a check taken out whole (an eviction's token matched before it reaps a part): which parts an eviction owns is the cache's (TASK-560)
quarantines-wait-for-every-vm-process: a filter taken out whole (the peers a run was staged to): whom a run waits for is the quarantine's (board 6208)
windows-listed-once-a-map: a set replaced by a list, a window entered a map: the window set's own choice (TASK-602)
